Read-only Explore is complete for the sole batch issue #36. Authenticated request SHA256 and complete index matched the clean baseline. Relevant code and contribution guidance were inspected; no source files changed and no compilation or tests ran. No competing implementation was found in the fresh exact-key and semantic issue/PR searches; the only matching upstream commit is the known test fixture. The compatibility/migration-policy gate is genuine, not merely missing RED evidence.

{
  "issues": [
    {
      "number": 36,
      "tag": "needs-a-human",
      "duplicate_of": null,
      "comment": "needs-a-human: the collision is confirmed, but validation timing and the compatibility policy must be settled before a regression test can define the intended fix.\n\nScope: UnionSubclassEntityPersister currently collapses sibling columns by Column identity before building the union; its constructor also precomputes superclass/subclass unions. Throwing there would reject the SessionFactory, including concrete loads that currently work.\n\nOne-way door: a new default mapping rejection changes which existing applications can start or query. It is not just a diagnostic-only patch.\n\nVerified against upstream 37616099b745e01500f65eb580f9cef270550cdb:\n- TablePerClassSiblingColumnTypeTest preserves concrete-subtype loading and marks only the polymorphic query as expected-failure; MySQL/MariaDB are explicitly skipped because they allow this mixed union. The fixture demonstrates the problem, not an agreed rejection contract.\n- Dialect.equivalentTypes is directional schema-validation/migration compatibility. Using a single ordered comparison would make acceptance depend on sibling iteration order; requiring mutual equivalence would reject widening integral pairs accepted in one direction. It is not an established UNION compatibility rule.\n- Runtime union generation chooses FILTER/TREAT branches, or returns the original full union for projection-only use. A query-time approach must validate the actual participating columns after pruning, cover both paths and non-SQM loaders, and preserve quoted identifiers and inherited columns.\n- HHH-20965 is separate full-support work, not a duplicate. This batch contains only #36; no duplicates are closed.\n\nPossible narrow direction: validate only a genuinely incompatible participating union at query time, before JDBC execution. This is a design candidate, not a verified complete patch location.\n\nGate: decide boot-time versus query-time rejection and whether portable rejection should apply to dialects that accept the union; define symmetric sibling compatibility and diagnostic exception semantics. Then add one focused RED test with concrete-load, compatible-numeric, quoted-name, inherited-column and pruned-union controls before production changes.\n\nRead-only inspection completed; no source edits, compilation or tests were run. No RED/GREEN claim is made. This gate is technical, not a request for user approval."
    }
  ],
  "patterns": "No duplicate pattern in this one-issue batch. Do not confuse directional schema compatibility with sibling UNION compatibility or validate precomputed unions before query pruning."
}

Source evidence: UnionSubclassEntityPersister.java constructor 156-168, column collection 549-563, pruning 635-696; TablePerClassSiblingColumnTypeTest.java 59-75; Dialect.java 1517-1555; ColumnDefinitions.java 32-52; Column.java 275-306; BaseSqmToSqlAstConverter.java 836-840; EntityUseUnionSubclassOptimizationTest.java 35-63. Query-time effective-union validation remains only a candidate requiring non-SQM loader coverage. Full mapping support is HHH-20965, out of scope.

